            <ArticleTitle>Primary cytomegalovirus infection, atypical Kawasaki disease, and coronary aneurysms in 2 infants.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e53-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We describe 2 infants who developed atypical Kawasaki disease and coronary aneurysms during primary cytomegalovirus infection. These observations suggest that children with coronary aneurysms and Kawasaki-like disease should be tested for cytomegalovirus. Conversely, children with unusually severe primary cytomegalovirus infection should be tested for coronary aneurysms.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
